; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 12, course 7 "Clockwork Keep": "Clockwork Keep" (SPEC.md 137.20)
;
; D major at 102.4 BPM, a GAVOTTE: a row is FOUR sub-ticks (`groove 4`, `unit
; 32`, so a 32nd is a row, 73 ms), a beat 32 sub-ticks, a bar of 4/4 128 and a
; pattern two bars, 4.7 s. Every phrase starts on the half bar, as a gavotte's
; does. The SECOND song written for this course (2026-11-25), from the course
; and not from the first, which the owner heard as "almost out of tune".
;
; The course is a castle that is one LOCK: three shut doors, each showing what
; opens it, and machines that make the player wait and then go. So the tune
; KNOCKS. Its motif is two notes up to the door, a turn, and two knocks - one
; note twice, short, each answered by the same note lower down:
;   a4 d4 | f+4 e8 d8  A4 A4 | b4 a8 g8  F+4 F+4 |        (over D A | G D/F+)
; The first phrase ends waiting on the dominant (the door is shut: E, held);
; the second is the same phrase with its key - the knock an octave up, on D -
; and it closes.
;
; Intro (2 bars): the DRAWBRIDGE lays down - eight planks, eight notes down
;    the scale from D4, an 8th each, the bass alone - and lands; then the two
;    notes up to the door.
; A  (8 bars), the harp, both hands: the gavotte, question and answer.
; B  (8 bars), the glockenspiel: the MACHINES, each behind the last. A run of
;    16ths and the bass's answer under it half a bar later - two rising (Bm
;    Em), two falling (A D) - then the answers come a BEAT behind (G A Bm), a
;    terraced fall of 16ths from G6, and the tune stops on F+, the dominant of
;    the relative minor.
; C  (4 bars), the music box: the TREASURY. Unbroken 8ths up and down one
;    chord a bar (Bm G Em A) over the organ's held pedal; no chord, no beat.
; A' (4 bars), the organ: the THRONE. The answer as a fanfare - a dotted climb
;    up the D chord to the high knock, a scale up to a close on D6 - and the
;    two notes up to the door again, into the loop.
; Intro, A B C A' for ever: the loop is 24 bars, 3,072 sub-ticks, 56.3 s.
;
; IN TUNE, by construction, and measured (KEEP.md section 16):
; - ONE scale, D major's seven notes, in every part of every bar. The minor
;   section is B minor with its A natural, so no note is ever raised in one
;   part while another has it plain; no accidental is written anywhere.
; - only the bank's PHASE-TRUE patches: harp, glockenspiel, music box, organ,
;   pedal. MEASURED on the tool's OPL2: the plucked patches with a strong
;   modulator and feedback (pluckbass, bass, lute, stab) drift as they decay -
;   the fundamental reads up to 34 cents flat in the bottom octave while its
;   second partial stays true, and the lute 17 - 28 cents flat in its attack -
;   and trumpet, horn, recorder, fiddle, strings and chip carry the chip's
;   vibrato. None of them is used; nor is a scoop or an arpeggio.
; - under the D of each pickup the chord is a bare fifth (E A E): a C+ there
;   is a minor ninth under the tune. No two parts are ever a semitone class
;   apart for longer than a passing 8th.
; - the drums the speaker blips are in the key: the kick falls from D, the
;   snare's snap is A to A. No tom (its fall is chromatic), no clap.
; - THE SPEAKER plays the bass only where the lead rests (`spkbass`), and
;   every bass note it can reach is D3 or above: below C3 its whole Hz are up
;   to 11 cents out (D2 -9.7, F+2 +9.5), from D3 up under 3. The bottom
;   octave is under sounding lead notes, where only the AdLib plays it.
; - what the speaker alternates is never a wrong note: a knock's answer is the
;   knock's own note lower, B's answers are the lead's own runs, and nothing
;   else is folded (the lead's other gaps are one sub-tick).
;
; The machines run on 128 and 256 game steps, and a step is a sub-tick: a bar
; is the stair's and the spikes' period, a pattern the bridges' and the cogs',
; and the loop is twelve of those, so the song keeps the castle's rate. Their
; PHASE is not tied (the song starts with the bracket, the play's counter with
; the play), so nothing here is written to land on a machine's beat.
;
; ON THE ADLIB the harp's and the harp bass's notes ring past their gates (a
; struck patch), so a knock's silence is the speaker's; the organ and the
; pedal are additive, so a `v` lowers only their fundamental stop.
; Every phrase names its instrument and volume where it differs from the
; voice's; the loop comes back to A, which starts from the voices.

song clockwork "Clockwork Keep"
groove 4
unit 32
rows 64
measure 32
spkbass
voice lead harp
voice bass harp
voice chord harp

; --- the intro: the drawbridge's eight planks, and the two notes to the door ----
lead LI  = r1 | r2 o4 v15 a4 >d4 |
bass BI  = v12 o4 l8 d c+ <b a g f+ e d | d4 a4 <a4 >e4 |
chord CI = r1 | o3 v7 [f+ a >d]2 [e a >e]2 |
drum DI  = v10 l8 h h h h h h h h | k4 h h h4 h4 |

; --- A: the gavotte. A knock is an 8th and an 8th's silence (q16), and the bass
; --- answers in the silence; the pickups' chord is a bare fifth (no C+ under D) ----
lead LA1 = o5 v15 f+:1 & g:1 & f+:6 e8 d8 q16 a4 a4 q1 | b4 a8 g8 q16 f+4 f+4 q1 |
lead LA2 = o5 v15 g4 f+8 e8 d4 c+4 | e2 o4 a4 >d4 |
lead LA3 = o5 v15 f+:1 & g:1 & f+:6 e8 d8 q16 >d4 d4 q1 | c+4 <b8 a8 b4 g4 |
lead LA4 = o5 v15 f+4 e8 d8 e4 c+4 | d2 r2 |
bass BA1 = v11 o3 d4 <d4 l8 a >a <a >a | <g4 >g4 l8 <f+ >f+ <f+ >f+ |
bass BA2 = v11 o3 e4 <e4 a4 >a4 | <a4 >e4 <a4 >e4 |
bass BA3 = v11 o3 d4 <d4 l8 >d >d <d a | o2 a4 >a4 g4 <g4 |
bass BA4 = v11 o3 f+4 <f+4 a4 >a4 | d4 <a4 >d4 f+4 |
chord CA1 = o3 v7 [f+ a >d]2 r2 | [g b >d]2 r2 |
chord CA2 = o3 v7 [g b >e]2 [e a >e]2 | [e a >c+]2 [e a >e]2 |
chord CA3 = o3 v7 [f+ a >d]2 r2 | [e a >c+]2 [g b >d]2 |
chord CA4 = o3 v7 [f+ a >d]2 [g a >c+]2 | [f+ a >d]2 r2 |
drum DA1 = v10 l8 h h h h k h k h | h h h h k h k h |
drum DK  = v10 l8 k h h h h h h h | k h h h h h h h |

; --- B: the machines, each behind the last: a run, and the bass's answer under
; --- it - half a bar behind, then a beat ----------------------------------------------
lead LB1 = @glock v12 o5 l16 f+ g a b >d8 <b8 r2 | b >c+ d e g8 e8 r2 |
lead LB2 = @glock v12 o5 l16 a g f+ e c+8 e8 r2 | >d c+ <b a f+8 a8 r2 |
lead LB3 = @glock v12 o5 l16 g a b >d r4 <a b >c+ e r4 | <b >c+ d f+ r4 e4 f+4 |
lead LB4 = @glock v12 o6 l16 g f+ e d e d c+ <b >c+ <b a g a g f+ e | c+4 e4 f+2 |
bass BB1 = v12 o2 b4 r4 o3 l16 f+ g a b >d8 <b8 | o2 e4 r4 o3 l16 b >c+ d e g8 e8 |
bass BB2 = v12 o2 a4 r4 o4 l16 a g f+ e c+8 e8 | o2 d4 r4 o4 l16 d c+ <b a f+8 a8 |
bass BB3 = v12 o2 g4 o3 l16 g a b >d o2 a4 o3 l16 a b >c+ e | o2 b4 o3 l16 b >c+ d f+ o2 a4 >a4 |
bass BB4 = v11 o2 e4 >e4 <a4 >a4 | <f+4 >c+4 <f+2 |
chord CB1 = o3 v8 [f+ b >d]4 r4 r2 | [g b >e]4 r4 r2 |
chord CB2 = o3 v8 [e a >c+]4 r4 r2 | [f+ a >d]4 r4 r2 |
chord CB3 = o3 v8 [g b >d]4 r4 [e a >c+]4 r4 | [f+ b >d]4 r4 [e a >c+]4 r4 |
chord CB4 = o3 v8 [g b >e]2 [g a >c+]2 | [f+ a >c+]1 |
drum DB3 = v10 l8 k h h h k h h h | k h h h k h h h |
drum DB4 = v10 l8 k h h h k h h h | k4 r4 r2 |

; --- C: the treasury - the music box over the organ's pedal, no chord, no beat -----
lead LC1 = @musicbox v8 o4 l8 q0 b >d f+ b >d <b f+ d | <b >d g b >d <b g d |
lead LC2 = @musicbox v8 o4 l8 q0 b >e g b >e <b g e | <a >c+ e a @organ v15 q1 <a4 >d4 |
bass BC1 = @pedal v8 o2 q0 b1 | g1 |
bass BC2 = @pedal v8 o2 q0 e1 | a2 @harp v11 q1 a4 >e4 |
chord CC2 = r1 | r2 o3 v7 [e a >e]2 |
drum DC2 = r1 | r2 v10 s4 s4 |

; --- A': the throne - the answer as a fanfare, on the organ ------------------------
lead LF1 = @organ v15 o5 f+8. f+16 a8 a8 q16 >d4 d4 q1 | c+4 <b8 a8 b4 g4 |
lead LF2 = @organ v15 o5 f+8 g8 a8 b8 >c+4 e4 | d2 @harp o4 a4 >d4 |
bass BF2 = v11 o2 f+4 >f+4 <a4 >a4 | d4 <d4 a4 >e4 |
chord CF1 = o3 v8 [f+ a >d]4 [f+ a >d]4 r2 | [e a >c+]4 [e a >c+]4 [g b >d]4 [g b >d]4 |
chord CF2 = o3 v8 [f+ a >d]4 [f+ a >d]4 [g a >c+]4 [g a >c+]4 | [f+ a >d]2 [e a >e]2 |
drum DF1 = v10 l8 k h s h k h k h | k h s h k h s h |

order LI  BI  CI  DI           ; 0: the intro
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA1          ; 1: A - the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DK
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DA1
order LA4 BA4 CA4 DK
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DK           ; B
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DK
order LB3 BB3 CB3 DB3
order LB4 BB4 CB4 DB4
order LC1 BC1 -   -            ; C
order LC2 BC2 CC2 DC2
order LF1 BA3 CF1 DF1          ; A'
order LF2 BF2 CF2 DF1
loop 1
